            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lkbolin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A very interesting recipe. It's not the North Carolina version of liver pudding though. NC liver pudding can be cut and fried, just as liver mush can. It's generally pretty solid though and can be eaten as a sandwich. \n\nThis liver pudding is like a cross between the liver pudding I knew and braunschweiger with a pudding-like consistency that's great served warm. It wasn't what I was looking for in a recipe, but it is GREAT. :-D",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-07T05:10:31.663Z"
          },
          {
